From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:33:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(startup): reserve MoE profile scratch before locking
 workspace arena

When patch 0849 skips profile_run under pinned kv_cache_memory_bytes, GPUModelRunner._reserve_profile_scratch previously only visited static_forward_context attention modules. On PP Stage 0 (no CED decoder attention layers) or low-TP/high-batch shapes, MoERunner workspace exceeds attention scratch and fails after WorkspaceManager.lock().

Walk model and draft modules for reserve_profile_scratch (passing max_num_tokens when accepted) and implement MoERunner.reserve_profile_scratch across decode, mid, and prefill tile tiers plus shared_experts and get_moe_output_buffer.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354

Rationale: Prevents WorkspaceManager locked-growth crashes on PP=2 Stage 0 and low-TP/high-batch shapes while keeping 0849 boot-time savings.

Quality: Startup workspace reservation only; zero numerical change.

Tests: pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v41_serving_contract.py (all passing on GB10).

Upstream-status: Local startup fix accompanying 0849.
